r back or butt up if you  struggle to keep your body in a straight  line and experience lower back pain when  performing a plank then start off by  doing plank with one knee bent this  plank variation helps to reduce the  pressure on your spine and puts more  tension on the abdominal muscles so it  helps to properly strengthen a core  without getting the lower back sore as  your core gets stronger that Gambel feet  and perform a normal plank raised leg  crunches raise leg crunches are much  more superior and lower back friendly  compared to regular crunches by keeping  your legs in a ninety degree position  this helps to deactivate the hip flexors  and keep the lower back flat against the  floor so there are no flexion or  extension happening in your lumbar spine  if the exercise is done correctly this  way your abs are forced to do all the  work if your neck is coming up first  watch out to avoid neck pain do not  place your hands behind your head  because this will tempt you to pull  forward and lift your neck up do not  jerk your head forward or use momentum  to lift yourself up  place your hands next to your head and  focus on engaging your core to lift  yourself off your head neck and apps  should be in one straight line and  remember as you crunch up engage your  core and aim to lift your shoulders off  the floor do not rush through the  movement use this exercise to develop a  promise  in your upper abs while reducing the  risk of lower back or neck pain  side plank we know that our core also  consists of the oblique muscles  hence we got to strengthen that as well  side plank is extremely effective to  target the obliques and lower back  that's in a forward plank hold position  slowly root it over to one side putting  the weight on your left arm and foot the  elbow should be directly under the  shoulder place your right arm on your  hip avoided sinking your hips down to  the ground because this can cause strain  in the lower back be sure to keep your  ab muscles tight and hips raised  throughout the exercise  hold this position for 15 to 20 seconds  and slowly rotate back to the starting  position and hold the side plank on the  other side if this gets too tough then  place your top leg in front as balanced  and the last workout is Superman  Superman is a great exercise to  strengthen the muscles along your spine  lie on his stomach legs straight out and  arms stretched overhead engage your ab  muscles and raise the opposite arm and  leg off the floor hold for three to five  breaths slowly and lower them down and  repeat on the opposite side continue  alternating for a total of 10 reps avoid  looking forward which will add extra  strain on your neck keep your neck in a  neutral position by looking down  throughout the exercise these are five  exercises which will strengthen your  core without adding the strain on your  lower back and neck be sure to LIKE this  video and share this video to someone  who might find it useful don't forget to  also subscribe to my youtube channel and  check out more workout videos fitness  tips as well as recipes right yeah all  the best
 

